          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "size": "Large",
            "weight": "Bolder",
            "text": "Washington is now policing permit delays: DOJ has opened a civil-rights investigation into how one New Jersey township handles handgun purchase permits.",
            "wrap": true,
            "spacing": "Small"
          },
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "text": "DOJ’s Civil Rights Division says it is investigating Pennsauken Township, N.J., over alleged delays in answering applications for handgun purchase permits; it says it has reached no conclusions. The same day, 174 House members asked DOJ to resume enforcing the under-21 handgun-sales ban.",
            "wrap": true,
            "spacing": "Small"
          },
